1354 (15) "Incapacitated" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75-1-201.
1355 (16) "Income" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75A-5-102.
1356 (17) "Interested person" means, except as provided in Section 75B-2-110, the same as that term is
defined in Section 75-1-102.
1358 (18) "Lease" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75-1-201.
1359 (19) "Minor" means an individual who is younger than 18 years old.
1360 (20) "Mortgage" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75-1-201.
1361 (21) "Nongeneral power of appointment" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75A-4-102.
1363 (22) "Organization" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75-1-201.
1364 (23) "Parent" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75-1-201.
1365 (24) "Person" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75-1-201.
1366 (25) "Personal representative" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75-1-201.
1367 (26) "Petition" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75-1-201.
1368 (27) "Power of appointment" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75A-4-102.
1369 (28) "Principal" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75A-5-102.
- 41 -

HB0176S02 compared with HB0176S03
1370 (29) "Property" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75-1-201.
1371 (30) "Protected person" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75-1-201.
1372 (31) "Record" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75-1-201.
1373 (32) "Security" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75-1-201.
1374 (33)
(a) "Settlor" means a person, including a testator, who creates, or contributes property to, a trust.
1376 (b) If more than one person creates or contributes property to a trust, each person is a settlor of the
portion of the trust property attributable to that person's contribution except to the extent another
person has the power to revoke or withdraw that portion.
1379 (34) "Sign" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75-1-201.
1380 (35) "State" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75-1-201.
1381 (36) "Successor" means a person, other than a creditor, that is entitled to property of a decedent under
the decedent's will or Title 75, Utah Uniform Probate Code.
1383 (37) "Testator" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75-1-201.
1384 (38)
(a) "Trust" means:
1385 (i) a health savings account, as defined in Section 223 of the Internal Revenue Code;
1386 (ii) an express trust, private or charitable, with additions thereto, wherever and however created; or
1388 (iii) a trust created or determined by judgment or decree under which the trust is to be administered
in the manner of an express trust.
1390 (b) "Trust" does not include:
1391 (i) a constructive trust;
1392 (ii) a resulting trust;
1393 (iii) a conservatorship;
1394 (iv) a personal representative;
1395 (v) a trust account as defined in Title 75, Chapter 6, Nonprobate Transfers;
1396 (vi) a custodial arrangement under Title 75A, Chapter 8, Uniform Transfers To Minors Act;
1398 (vii) a business trust providing for certificates to be issued to beneficiaries;
1399 (viii) a common trust fund;
1400 (ix) a voting trust;
1401 (x) a preneed funeral plan under Title 58, Chapter 9, Funeral Services Licensing Act;
- 42 -

HB0176S02 compared with HB0176S03
1402 (xi) a security arrangement;
1403 (xii) a liquidation trust;
1404 (xiii) a trust for the primary purpose of paying debts, dividends, interest, salaries, wages, profits,
pensions, or employee benefits of any kind; or
1406 (xiv) any arrangement under which a person is nominee or escrowee for another person.
1408 (39) "Trust company" means the same as that term is defined in Section [7-5-1] 7-5-101.
1409 (40) "Trustee" means an original, additional, and successor trustee, and cotrustee, whether or not
appointed or confirmed by the court.
1411 (41) "Trust instrument" means an instrument executed by the settlor that contains terms of the trust,
including any amendments thereto.
1413 (42) "Ward" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75-1-201.
1414 (43) "Will" means the same as that term is defined in Section 75-1-201.
1313 Section 27. Section 75B-3-107 is amended to read:
1314 75B-3-107. Limitations on trust director.
1417 (1) A trust director is subject to the same rules as a trustee in a like position and under similar
circumstances in the exercise or nonexercise of a power of direction or further power under
Subsection 75B-3-106(2)(a) regarding:
1420 [(1)] (a) a payback provision in the terms of a trust necessary to comply with the Medicaid
reimbursement requirements in Section 1917 of the Social Security Act, 42 U.S.C. Sec. 1396p(d)(4)
(A), as amended, and any related regulations; and
1423 [(2)] (b) a charitable interest in the trust, including notice regarding the interest to the attorney general.
1425 (2) A trust director may not engage in trust business, as that term is defined in Section 7-5-101.
1325 Section 28. Effective date.
Effective Date.
This bill takes effect on May 6, 2026.
